WEBVTT

00:00:28.672 --> 00:00:31.352
Why are they all staring at us?

00:00:31.512 --> 00:00:33.872
Maybe they think you look funny.

00:00:36.512 --> 00:00:37.832
(CHUCKLES)

00:00:39.032 --> 00:00:41.672
Stop your fussing. You look lovely.

00:01:00.792 --> 00:01:02.912
We have come to see Aslan.

00:01:03.312 --> 00:01:05.792
(CROWD MURMURING)

00:01:47.152 --> 00:01:50.152
Welcome, Peter, Son of Adam.

00:01:50.352 --> 00:01:53.672
Welcome, Susan and Lucy,
Daughters of Eve.

00:01:54.432 --> 00:01:57.912
And welcome to you, Beavers.
You have my thanks.

00:01:58.112 --> 00:02:00.112
But where is the fourth?

00:02:01.672 --> 00:02:03.992
That's why we're here, sir.

00:02:04.592 --> 00:02:06.152
We need your help.

00:02:06.312 --> 00:02:08.992
We had a little trouble along the way.

00:02:09.792 --> 00:02:11.632
Our brother's been captured
by the White Witch.

00:02:11.832 --> 00:02:14.672
Captured? How could this happen?

00:02:16.272 --> 00:02:19.392
He betrayed them, Your Majesty.

00:02:19.552 --> 00:02:20.592
(CROWD MURMURS)

00:02:20.752 --> 00:02:23.672
-Then he has betrayed us all!
-Peace, Oreius.

00:02:24.632 --> 00:02:27.032
I'm sure there's an explanation.

00:02:29.512 --> 00:02:31.432
It's my fault, really.

00:02:33.112 --> 00:02:35.072
I was too hard on him.

00:02:39.312 --> 00:02:40.712
We all were.

00:02:41.592 --> 00:02:43.432
Sir, he's our brother.

00:02:43.592 --> 00:02:45.272
I know, dear one.

00:02:45.592 --> 00:02:48.752
But that only makes
the betrayal all the worse.

00:02:49.472 --> 00:02:52.032
This may be harder than you think.

00:02:57.472 --> 00:02:59.232
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:02:59.392 --> 00:03:03.832
That is Cair Paravel,
the castle of the four thrones.

00:03:05.272 --> 00:03:08.752
In one of which you will sit, Peter,
as High King.

00:03:10.472 --> 00:03:12.552
You doubt the prophecy?

00:03:12.712 --> 00:03:15.512
No. That's just it.

00:03:17.552 --> 00:03:20.272
Aslan, I'm not what you all think I am.

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:23.152
Peter Pevensie, formerly of Finchley.

00:03:24.512 --> 00:03:28.672
Beaver also mentioned that you
planned on turning him into a hat.

00:03:29.872 --> 00:03:31.192
(BOTH CHUCKLING)

00:03:31.952 --> 00:03:36.952
Peter, there is a Deep Magic,
more powerful than any of us,

00:03:37.112 --> 00:03:39.432
that rules over all of Narnia.

00:03:39.632 --> 00:03:42.032
It defines right from wrong,

00:03:42.192 --> 00:03:44.592
and governs all our destinies.

00:03:44.752 --> 00:03:47.552
Yours, and mine.

00:03:48.312 --> 00:03:49.992
But I couldn't even
protect my own family.

00:03:50.152 --> 00:03:52.712
You've brought them safely this far.

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:55.312
Not all of them.

00:03:55.472 --> 00:03:59.072
Peter, I will do what I can
to help your brother,

00:03:59.792 --> 00:04:02.792
but I need you to consider
what I ask of you.

00:04:04.832 --> 00:04:07.352
I, too, want my family safe.

00:04:10.392 --> 00:04:13.592
Is our little prince uncomfortable?

00:04:14.352 --> 00:04:17.032
Does he want his pillow fluffed?

00:04:19.912 --> 00:04:23.392
Special treatment for the special boy!

00:04:25.472 --> 00:04:27.792
Isn't that what you wanted?

00:04:30.592 --> 00:04:32.352
LUCY: You look like Mum.

00:04:32.552 --> 00:04:35.992
Mum hasn't had a dress like this
since before the war.

00:04:36.712 --> 00:04:40.352
We should bring her one back.
A whole trunk full!

00:04:42.272 --> 00:04:44.032
If we ever get back.

00:04:48.032 --> 00:04:50.112
I'm sorry I'm like that.

00:04:51.752 --> 00:04:54.512
We used to have fun together,
didn't we?

00:04:55.032 --> 00:04:58.192
Yes. Before you got boring.

00:04:58.352 --> 00:04:59.352
(LAUGHING)

00:04:59.512 --> 00:05:00.952
Oh, really?

00:05:03.472 --> 00:05:04.992
(GIGGLING)

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.512
(GROWLING)

00:05:13.672 --> 00:05:14.672
(SCREAMING)

00:05:14.832 --> 00:05:16.032
Please don't try to run.

00:05:16.272 --> 00:05:19.752
-We're tired.
-And we'd prefer to kill you quickly.

00:05:19.912 --> 00:05:22.032
(SNARLING)

00:05:23.432 --> 00:05:24.672
(HORN BLOWING) (HORN BLOWING)

00:05:24.832 --> 00:05:26.232
Susan!

00:05:35.792 --> 00:05:37.192
Get back!

00:05:37.952 --> 00:05:39.192
Peter!

00:05:41.952 --> 00:05:43.312
Come on.

00:05:44.312 --> 00:05:47.032
We've already been
through this before.

00:05:47.192 --> 00:05:49.672
We both know you haven't got it in you.

00:05:49.832 --> 00:05:51.672
Peter! Watch out!

00:06:00.752 --> 00:06:04.872
No! Stay your weapons.
This is Peter's battle.

00:06:06.872 --> 00:06:09.072
You may think you're a king,

00:06:09.232 --> 00:06:11.392
but you're going to die

00:06:11.552 --> 00:06:13.592
-like a dog!
-LUCY: Look out!

00:06:14.072 --> 00:06:15.472
Peter!

